#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
agent.py — a minimal, dependency-free agentic command runner for Linux.

Runs a ReAct loop: the model proposes ONE shell command at a time, the agent runs
it, feeds the output back, and repeats until the task is done.

Two backends for talking to the model:
  * api  (default) — posts directly to the OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint (the SAME
    API your `ask` shell function calls), via Python's stdlib urllib. Run :setup once.
  * ask           — shells out to your existing `ask` bash function (bash -ic 'ask'),
    flattening the conversation into a single prompt. Use --backend ask.

Safety model (defense in depth):
  * A local, deterministic classifier scans every command BEFORE it runs.
  * Proven local reads run automatically. Default mode asks for every other action;
    auto mode still asks for the danger tier (and for structured edits of sensitive
    files) and refuses it in --non-interactive unless an anchored --allow matches.
  * Child commands run with the invoking user's host permissions but never inherit
    provider credentials or secret-like variables.
  * The model's own risk self-assessment is merged in (whichever is higher wins).

Reliability aids (for weaker/flash models):
  * Premature-finish guard: won't accept a "finish" before a real command has run.
  * Loop-breaker: refuses to re-run a recently executed command; bails after repeats.
  * Auto-heal: on a failed command, automatically runs READ-ONLY diagnostic probes
    (e.g. for "command not found", missing files/units/containers, permission denied)
    and feeds the findings back so the model can pick a working command. Probes never
    mutate state and are skipped if they would be anything but read-only.

Requires: Python 3.8+, /bin/bash. No third-party Python packages.

Environment:
  GENAI_KEY       (optional override) bearer token for the API; otherwise use :setup
  GENAI_URL       (optional)  default https://api.genai.mil/v1/chat/completions
  GENAI_MODEL     (optional)  default gemini-3.1-pro-preview
  GENAI_CA        (optional)  path to a CA bundle (for internal/.mil CAs)
  GENAI_INSECURE  (deprecated) also requires --insecure acknowledgment
  GENAI_TIMEOUT   (optional)  total seconds for one model turn, including retries (default 90)
  GENAI_BACKEND   (optional)  "api" (default) or "ask"
  GENAI_BETA_KEY  (optional override) bearer token for the GenAI beta proxy
  GENAI_BETA_URL  (optional)  default https://api-beta.genai.mil/v1/chat/completions
  GENAI_BETA_MODEL (optional) default gemini-2.5-pro; run :models for the live list
  ACT_CONFIG      (optional)  alternate per-user setup file path
  ACT_MODEL_DISCOVERY (optional) 1 (default) = query the provider's live /models list at
                  startup when a key is set; 0 disables the startup query
  ACT_TOOLS       (optional)  default 1: send the action protocol as a native tool/function
                  schema so the endpoint enforces it. Endpoints that reject tools are
                  detected (HTTP 400/422) and fall back to JSON mode automatically
  ACT_PLAN_MODEL  (optional)  plan with this model id, then execute the steps on
                  GENAI_MODEL (also --plan-model / :planmodel; outranks ACT_RACE)
  ACT_RACE        (optional)  1 = send the planning turn to all available models, wait for
                  every answer, and have the ACTIVE model judge them (pick the best or
                  merge) and execute the task (also --race / :race). Costs one request per
                  model plus a judge turn
  ACT_RACE_MODELS (optional)  comma-separated model ids to race (default: all available)
  ACT_RACE_GRACE  (optional)  default 30: once most racers have answered (and at least two
                  usable plans are in), stragglers get this many more seconds before they
                  are dropped as "too slow"; 0 = wait for every model up to GENAI_TIMEOUT
  ACT_JSON_MODE   (optional)  default 1: ask the endpoint for a JSON object response
  ACT_PREFILL     (optional)  default 1: seed the reply with '{' to force bare JSON
                  (endpoints that reject either are detected and it is dropped automatically)
  ACT_ALLOW       (optional)  pre-approved `run` command patterns, one regex per line (also
                  --allow, repeatable). Each must match the WHOLE command; only plain single
                  commands qualify, never a catastrophic payload. With --non-interactive this is
                  an allowlist-only fix mode for automation (e.g. Ansible)
  ACT_RESULT_FILE (optional)  write a JSON summary of a one-shot run here on every exit path
                  (also --result-file); schema act.result/1, see docs/RESULT_FILE.md
  ACT_PSEUDONYMIZE (optional) default 1: replace host names, domain names, IP addresses,
                  user names and e-mail addresses with placeholders (host-N, domain-N.invalid,
                  198.18.x.x, user-N) in everything sent to the model, and translate the
                  model's replies back before anything runs. 0 (or --no-pseudonymize, or
                  "pseudonymize": false in the config file) sends them as they are. ':pseudo
                  show' lists the mapping. Best effort: a short host name ACT cannot recognize
                  (not this host, not in /etc/hosts, not listed) is sent as written
  ACT_PSEUDO_NAMES (optional) extra host/server names to mask, comma-separated (also
                  --pseudo-name, or "pseudo_names" in the config file)
  ACT_TOKEN_PARAM (optional)  output-limit field name: max_tokens or max_completion_tokens.
                  Default: auto — newer OpenAI models (gpt-5*, o-series, Ask Sage gpt-5-gov)
                  reject max_tokens with HTTP 400; the swap is detected per endpoint.
  ACT_API_FORMAT  (optional)  auto (default), openai or anthropic, for every provider. ACT
                  speaks two request formats: OpenAI chat/completions (the provider URL) and
                  the Anthropic Messages API (the same URL ending in /messages). auto tries
                  the model's usual format first and switches when the endpoint refuses the
                  model, then remembers the choice per model (':probe' tests both)
  GENAI_ANTHROPIC_URL / GENAI_BETA_ANTHROPIC_URL / ASKSAGE_ANTHROPIC_URL (optional)
                  the provider's Anthropic Messages URL. Default: its URL with
                  /chat/completions replaced by /messages
  ACT_ALLOW_HTTP  (optional)  1 = allow a plain http:// provider URL to a non-loopback host
                  (default: https only; http is accepted for localhost). Redirects are never
                  followed, so the API key can not be forwarded to another host
  The full list of variables (limits, debug, theme, ...) is in README.md.
"""

